# Both Dockerfiles do `COPY . .` in the builder stage. Without this file Docker
# ships the entire repo as build context: host node_modules (often Linux-incompatible
# native binaries like bcrypt built on Windows), full .git history, stale build
# outputs, and — critically — .env secrets. Keep the context lean and safe.

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image via pnpm install)
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build outputs (regenerated inside the image)
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
apps/api/public
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS & tooling
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Environment / secrets — never copy into an image
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Tests, reports, coverage
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__tests__
apps/web/e2e
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/playwright-report
apps/web/.playwright
coverage

# Docs & installer artifacts (not needed at build time)
docs
installer/bundle
installer/output
BUG_REPORT.md
MemoryManual.md
*.md

# Local data / logs
.docker-data
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker meta itself
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
